      "writtenOn": "2017-02-17T01:44:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027re using pathless guards pretty much everywhere.  For example, board.h does too, and so do the headers in drivers/.\n\nThe makefile ensures that only one chip directory gets included, so this is pretty safe.\n\nI wouldn\u0027t object to fully-pathing them starting with __CROS_EC.  Bonus points for doing it with a clever python script so it doesn\u0027t have to be done by hand.  But be careful; we\u0027ve gotten way too clever with macros and multiply-included headers for our own good.  Maybe file a P3 bug to do that?",
